vectors.json: ground truth for muster's model of the LEZ multisig on LEZ v0.3.0 (lez/multisig.nim
with layout v0.3, the v0.3 instructions in lez/tx.nim).

It was generated by the v0.3 port's own crate, multisig_core, the types its program
(run_program(plan, apply), no SPEL) reads and writes: the binary `vectors` in the port's
e2e_v03 package (src/bin/vectors.rs). The port is a clone of logos-co/lez-multisig, branch
feat/lee-v0.3.0, commit 8cd448d (exo-eb6.4.4; docs/design/lez-multisig-v03.md), to be
offered upstream (exo-eb6.4.4.5).

Regenerate it in the port (build needs as in infra/lez/localnet.sh's header: a C++
compiler, libclang; a binary built with nixpkgs#gcc also needs nix's libstdc++ to run):

  RISC0_SKIP_BUILD=1 cargo build --release -p e2e_v03 --bin vectors
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<nixpkgs#gcc.cc^lib>/lib target/release/vectors > vectors.json

Generated 2026-10-01.

What it pins, for a program account 0x11…, create key 0x22…, members 0x01…/0x02…/0x03…, and a
recipient 0x0e…:
- the PDAs: state (the create key as its one seed), proposal #1 and #2
  (SHA-256("multisig_prop___" ‖ create key ‖ index LE)), the vault
  (SHA-256("multisig_vault__" ‖ create key)), each SHA-256("/LEE/v0.2/AccountId/PDA/" padded ‖
  program account ‖ seed);
- MultisigState borsh (v0.2.4's layout: create key, threshold u8, member_count u8, members,
  transaction_index u64 = the last proposal's index);
- Proposal borsh with each commitment: Call(TargetCall { program account, shard selectors
  as (account, program) pairs, instruction bytes, pda seeds }) and Config(ConfigAction);
  status Active | Executed;
- the call's Commitment hash (SHA-256("/lez-multisig/v0.3/Commitment/" padded ‖ borsh));
- every Instruction's borsh: CreateMultisig, Propose, ProposeConfig (each ConfigAction),
  Approve, Reject, Execute { approvers, call }, ExecuteConfig { approvers, action };
- the native token program's Transfer { amount: 100 } the call carries.
